  "comment": "The Akai MPC skin's layout (mpc/tools/make_skin.py renders it into mpc/skins/). keys: the MPC's six function keys under the screen, each a list of its pages (pressing the key again shows its next page). A page: two panels, one above the other; each panel is one Q-Link group of four (the top panel Q-Links 13-16, the lower one 9-12; bank direction RowTopDown, so a four-knob MPC banks to the top panel first) and holds four cards (a card: a parameter by name, its label, and 'bi' for a knob centred on zero, 'wide' for a card two columns wide). A panel's header carries its title and caption, a lamp (lit while 'lamp' is on), segmented switches ('switch': one or a list; touch) and a menu ('menu', touch; a double tap opens the list). program: the Program Mode Q-Links, the 16 most-used parameters by name, Q-Link 1..16 (1 = bottom left, 13 = top left).",
